Article 10 The competent department of commerce under the State Council may, jointly with other relevant departments of the State such as foreign affairs and customs, assess the countries and regions of destination for the export of dual-use items by taking into account the following factors, determine the risk levels, and adopt corresponding control measures:
(1) the impact on national security and interests;
(2) the need to fulfill international obligations such as non-proliferation;
(3) the need to implement treaties and agreements concluded or acceded to by China;
(4) the need to implement relevant binding resolutions and measures adopted by the United Nations Security Council; and
(5) other factors that need to be considered.

Article 39 Any export operator who commits any of the following acts shall be punished in accordance with Article 34 of the Export Control Law:
(1) exporting dual-use items without permission;
(2) exporting dual-use items beyond the scope, conditions, or validity period specified in the export license;
(3) exporting dual-use items the export of which is prohibited;
(4) circumventing the licensing requirement for exporting dual-use items by means such as modification, splitting into parts or components; or
(5) using a license in violation of the provisions to export dual-use items under the circumstances specified in Article 18 of these Regulations.
